From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: natemu <natemu@example.invalid>
Date: Tue, 27 Oct 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 6/9] FEXCore: slice1 precision (state and effects at each
 access site)

Every change is guarded by fexc_slice1; predicates live in
tools/fexc/shim/fexc_precision.h. Goal: at a guest memory access the guest
state is the state before its instruction and none of its effects is
committed.

RedundantFlagCalculationElimination: every guest memory op reads all six
flags (no flag write before it is deleted or narrowed), and so does the
GuestOpcode of an instruction that has an access (the incoming flags are live
at the instruction start even if the instruction itself invalidates some);
InvalidateFlags stays a write (an undefined value, so an earlier write may
die), a guest load with a dead value is kept, and an instruction with an NZCV
write before one of its accesses saves its incoming NZCV to the frame
(LoadNZCV + StoreContext after its GuestOpcode).

RegisterAllocationPass: a guest memory op and an instruction boundary count
as an access of every static register, so a value is coalesced into its
static register only if no access lies between its definition and its
store; a load's own value never gets a static register (a pop keeps its
writeback stack pointer in RSP's register); TryPostRAMerge's candidate is
reset at GuestOpcode (no push/pop pair across instructions); a kept load
with no uses frees its register at once.
